STAGE 1 Fixing themes:
----------------------
1) Right now the app does not compile because I changed the presets.rs and some colors are empty and some are missing the alpha channel so instead of 8 they are 6 letters.
rgba() function should accept both uppercase and lowercase input. Should accept empty string or 6 characters or 8 characters. We should remove the "#" from all colors.

2) Make theme colors configurable within the app itself with #RGBA format, if alpha is omitted then rgba() function should use FF automatically. If the user misses the "#" we automatically add it for the GUI text box, but we don't use it in the config.toml. If the user includes the colors with the "#" we accept it for the GUI, but strip it off for the config.toml.
There should be a toggle for each button color group saying: "accent" which will inherit the desktop accent color for the resting fill color of that color group and also disable the input text box for the resting fill color.
Somehow we need to make this work with the rgba() function and saving the color in the config.toml, so maybe we need another function that handles the accent color automatic update, I'm not sure.

2) Rename themes to color schemes in the settings GUI and rename "debug_raw_formula" to "ascii_mode" in config.toml

3) I have changed the application name from cosmic calc to "CalcRS" . Please update all documentation, comments, source code that refers to cosmic calc. But of course we still use libcosmic.

4) Color schemes:
Remove "Texas" and "Tokyo" color schemes
Add "Army" with "ArmyChalk" font and green/brown color palette with white text
Add "Matrix" with "JetBrains Mono" font and green #53dc52 color over black background
Add "Sandstone" with "Roboto Slab" font and color palette: #D0C9BF #C4BBAE #BAAB9B #AB9680 #998570 #876E56
Add "Monokai" with "Noto Sans Math" font and color palette: #272822 #f8f8f2 #878b9180 #1e1f1c #3e3d32 #90908a #414339 #464741 #f8f8f2 #ccccc7 #e6db74 #464741 #fd971f #e6db74 #f92672 #a6e22e
Add "Inherit Desktop" should auto detect the system's general font. This color scheme should be the default color scheme option when we start the application the first time and config.toml gets generated. It should be on top of the color scheme list and should inherit the colors from the KDE, Gnome, Cosmic, Xfce desktop

5) Restructure the color definitions in presets.rs to include the 2nd toggled (alt) state for every button group and make it more compact by removing the "#" from the color codes. I want a very compact color definition table so please change the rgba to accept two colors like this (also change the header comments to include ",alt"):
```
number: ButtonColors::grid(
                //                     resting,alt                hover,alt                  pressed,alt
                StateColors::new(rgba("E0E0E0FF,E0E0E0"), rgba("F7F7F7,F7F7F7FF"), rgba("CACACAFF,F7F7FF")), // fill
                StateColors::new(rgba("FFFFFFFF,FFFFFFFF"), rgba("FFFFFFFF,FFFFFF"), rgba("FFFFFFFF,")), // label
                StateColors::new(rgba(","), rgba(",FFFFFFFF"), rgba("FFFFFFFF,")), // border
```
Be prepared for missing values, we need to have a fallback mechanism. If the alt color is missing e.g.: StateColors::new(rgba("E0E0E0FF,") then just use the primary color for alt
Similarly if the primary is missing e.g.: StateColors::new(rgba(",E0E0E0FF") then just use the alt color for the primary
If both are missing, then fallback to another group. Here is the fallback priority:
  toprow -> delete
  percent -> delete
  delete -> science
  second -> science
  bracket -> science
  rand -> science
  trig -> science
  reciprocal -> science
  science -> number
  equals -> basicop
  basicop -> number
  negate -> number
  decimal -> number
  At the end: number colors need to be defined because that's where all falls back
  It should work with multiple levels of fallback: e.g.: if no percent color defined (neither normal nor alt): fallback to delete, if no delete color defined, fallback to science, if no science color defined either: fallback to number, if number does not have alt color defined: fallback we use the primary color
  This way we can leave most of the colors empty in a theme, while still having the ability to color some groups separately if we want to
  I hope I didn't miss any button group from the fallback rules

6) Rearrange the color definitions in presets.rs to have the following order and use the same order in the GUI for the color group definition text boxes and in config.toml as well:
number
decimal
negate
basicop
equals
science
delete
percent
second
bracket
toprow
rand
trig
reciprocal

7) Save all color schemes in config.toml when the app launches the first time and just define which color scheme is the active. The user is allowed to change the color schemes from within the GUI but not the names of them.

